          type: 'folder',
          title: 'CHIRP',
          description:
            'Climate Hazard Center InfraRed Precipitation  (CHIRP) is a global (50&deg; S - 50&deg; N, 180&deg; E - 180&deg; W), 0.05&deg; resolution, 1981 to near-present gridded precipitation time series. CHIRP is produced 2 days after every pentad of the month and is not blended with any station values, it is based solely on satellite measurements. <br>See <a  target=\"_blank\"href="http://chc.ucsb.edu/data/chirps"> CHIRPS web page </a> for more information.',
          expanded: false,
